# A blocked presenter cannot prevent urgent shutdown.
@phase 1.2
> Manta {{VERSION}} by Miloslav Macurek
! block-stdout
< frobnicate
< quit
! exit 0 within 1000ms
---
# Search progress is droppable, but a completed search must survive a slow reader.
@phase 6.3
> Manta {{VERSION}} by Miloslav Macurek
! block-stdout
< position startpos
< go movetime 150
! sleep 250ms
! unblock-stdout
! allow-info begin
> {{BESTMOVE_LINE}}
! allow-info end
< quit
! exit 0 within 1000ms

---

# Quit exits within a bound even when required output has filled the queue behind a stalled reader.
# Streamed bench rows are required lines, so forty short reports exceed the pipe and the queue on
# every supported platform while the command mailbox never fills.
@phase 6.3
> Manta {{VERSION}} by Miloslav Macurek
! block-stdout
< bench 1
! sleep 25ms
< bench 1
! sleep 25ms
< bench 1
! sleep 25ms
< bench 1
! sleep 25ms
< bench 1
! sleep 25ms
< bench 1
! sleep 25ms
< bench 1
! sleep 25ms
